# Destined Confrontation sacrifices nothing until every player has chosen (CR 101.4, the ruling: "all the creatures not chosen
# are sacrificed simultaneously"). Bot1, the active player, keeps none of its Memnite; Bot2 then chooses with the graveyards
# still empty, so its Tarmogoyf is a 0/1 and it keeps the Tarmogoyf and four Memnites (total power 4). Had Bot1's Memnite been
# sacrificed first, an artifact creature card in a graveyard would have made the Tarmogoyf a 2/3 and the five a total of 6.
# Afterwards the Memnite (artifact, creature) and the sorcery are in graveyards: the Tarmogoyf is a 3/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Memnite
Plains
Plains
Destined Confrontation
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Tarmogoyf
Memnite
Memnite
Memnite
Memnite
Forest x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Tarmogoyf.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Destined Confrontation.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Tarmogoyf.Power = 0
Bot1.Choose()
Bot2.Choose(Tarmogoyf; Memnite; Memnite; Memnite; Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby
Bot1.Graveyard = Destined Confrontation; Memnite
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Tarmogoyf; Memnite; Memnite; Memnite; Memnite
Bot2.Battlefield.Tarmogoyf.Power = 3
